1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,810
Your phone just buzzed in your pocket...

2
00:00:02,130 --> 00:00:03,580
but nobody called.

3
00:00:03,880 --> 00:00:05,200
You check. Nothing.

4
00:00:06,040 --> 00:00:07,800
If that's happened to you, you're not

5
00:00:07,800 --> 00:00:08,500
alone.

6
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:10,760
In one hospital survey, sixty-eight

7
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:12,020
percent of the staff had felt these

8
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:14,400
phantom buzzes. In a study of students,

9
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,840
eighty-nine percent.

10
00:00:16,140 --> 00:00:18,360
The likely reason: your brain is waiting

11
00:00:18,360 --> 00:00:20,670
for that buzz, so it plays it safe.

12
00:00:20,980 --> 00:00:22,900
A tiny muscle twitch, or your clothes

13
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:24,820
rubbing your skin, and your brain shouts:

14
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,730
phone!

15
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:28,230
So... did your phone just buzz?
